ink an excessive and  clinically very dangerous amount of  coffee to experience any adverse effects  it's also worth noting that we are  exposed to mycotoxins from food that we  eat every single day including nuts  fruits whole grains spices chocolate and  even human breast milk and we also  discussed the whole glyphic thing it's  not a major concern I think that um the  bioavailability of animal protein is  just like next level I feel like I was  eating a lot of foods that just weren't  sticking like your body just doesn't  want to accept it it can have so many  grams of one particular nutrient but if  your body doesn't know what to do with  it well good luck when you eat eggs  organs when you're eating meat you are  actually eating something the body knows  what to do with what's something sounds  vague and made up like this it's because  it probably is  why you always lying yes it's true that  certain nutrients like iron are more  bioavailable from animal sources  compared to plant-based sources but the  body is well equipped to digest and  absorb nutrients from All Foods assuming  you don't have of an intolerance allergy  sensitivity or gut disorder that impairs  the digestion of that specific food  there is no evidence or even  hypothetical reason why your body would  know what to do with organ meat but not  know what to do with broccoli folks our  bodies are smart as oh this is this is a  really good one did your diet change  help your Endo symptoms like my hormones  are in such a better place so to bring  it all together here's my professional  opinion on why taddy likely feels her  best self on this flexible carnivore  diet for one by eliminating vegetables  and gluten containing foods she's  completely limited her exposure to high  FODMAP Foods a small number of which may  be exacerbating her digestive symptoms  however this would be far from the best  long-term diet for endometriosis  management fiber and antioxidants and  vegetables in whole grains actual